WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.157 --> 00:00:02.674
- Mind you, I've never seen
fashion magazines in my life.

00:00:02.674 --> 00:00:05.092
I've never worn makeup,
or heels, for that matter.

00:00:05.092 --> 00:00:08.105
In our industry, there's
where you make money,

00:00:08.105 --> 00:00:09.776
and the rest of it is fluff.

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:12.726
I think change is very good,

00:00:12.726 --> 00:00:15.179
regardless in what shape
or form it comes into it.

00:00:15.179 --> 00:00:16.980
Don't wait for the job to come to you,

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:18.221
you create the job.

00:00:18.221 --> 00:00:20.096
And, one of the reasons I
came to the United States

00:00:20.096 --> 00:00:21.910
was actually to experience life.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:23.656
The IMAN Home is my passion.

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:26.039
I love, I love interior decorating.

00:00:26.039 --> 00:00:27.873
It's not what you
achieve or what you gain,

00:00:27.873 --> 00:00:30.552
it's what you really
inspire other peoples to do.

00:00:30.552 --> 00:00:32.211
I didn't want the old mentality

00:00:32.211 --> 00:00:34.390
that the whole world is black and white,

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:36.099
because the world is not black and white.

00:00:36.099 --> 00:00:37.425
Always know your worth.

00:00:37.425 --> 00:00:38.549
Don't ever settle for less.

00:00:38.549 --> 00:00:40.815
I wanted, really, to create a book

00:00:40.815 --> 00:00:43.632
that really celebrated,
and a way to show it,

00:00:43.632 --> 00:00:46.925
that we are here, and
we are very beautiful.

00:00:46.925 --> 00:00:48.991
(upbeat music)

00:00:48.991 --> 00:00:51.963
- She's a Somali fashion model,
actress, and entrepreneur.

00:00:51.963 --> 00:00:54.421
A pioneer in the field
of ethnic cosmetics,

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:56.456
she's also known for her charitable work.

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:58.931
As of 2010, IMAN Cosmetics

00:00:58.931 --> 00:01:01.843
is a $25 million a year business.

00:01:01.843 --> 00:01:03.283
She's Iman Abdulmajid,

00:01:03.283 --> 00:01:05.909
and here are her top
ten rules for success.

00:01:05.909 --> 00:01:08.892
(rocket blasting)

00:01:08.892 --> 00:01:11.475
(upbeat music)

00:01:14.132 --> 00:01:15.783
And then, one day, lo and behold,

00:01:15.783 --> 00:01:18.003
while I was crossing on
my way to the campus,

00:01:18.003 --> 00:01:21.003
this photographer by the
name Peter Beard stopped me,

00:01:21.003 --> 00:01:24.152
and said, "Have you ever
been photographed before?"

00:01:24.152 --> 00:01:26.574
Mind you, I've never seen
fashion magazines in my life.

00:01:26.574 --> 00:01:29.160
I've never worn makeup,
or heels, for that matter,

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:32.144
so I had no idea what
he was talking about.

00:01:32.144 --> 00:01:34.693
But I thought, "Oh, God,
here we go, another white man

00:01:34.693 --> 00:01:36.866
"who thinks Africans have
never seen a camera before,

00:01:36.866 --> 00:01:38.316
or never before photographed."

00:01:38.316 --> 00:01:39.615
I said, "Yes, I have."

00:01:39.615 --> 00:01:40.812
And he said, "What magazine?"

00:01:40.812 --> 00:01:43.347
And I said, "My parents". (claps hands)

00:01:43.347 --> 00:01:46.487
And he said, "I'd like
to take your pictures."

00:01:46.487 --> 00:01:49.683
And, as I walked, kept on walking,

00:01:49.683 --> 00:01:50.945
he said the magic word.

00:01:50.945 --> 00:01:52.945
He said, "I'll pay you."

00:01:54.107 --> 00:01:56.038
And I said, "Well, how much?"

00:01:56.038 --> 00:01:57.937
He said, "Well, how much do you want?"

00:01:57.937 --> 00:02:00.816
And, I arrived there and there,
on the streets of Nairobi,

00:02:00.816 --> 00:02:04.097
on my way to campus, I made
my first modeling transaction.

00:02:04.097 --> 00:02:05.355
And, I said, "$8,000"

00:02:05.355 --> 00:02:07.653
because that was the tuition. (laughs)

00:02:07.653 --> 00:02:09.930
And, a couple of months later,

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:12.389
he brought the pictures to America,

00:02:12.389 --> 00:02:14.249
and they called for me,

00:02:14.249 --> 00:02:16.105
and, I have been here since then.

00:02:16.105 --> 00:02:20.105
And, I wanted what I
called "the spoils of war".

00:02:21.078 --> 00:02:25.130
Because, in our industry,
there's where you make money,

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:27.600
and the rest of it is fluff.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:31.310
What you do in what's called
"editorial" in the magazines,

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:33.618
they pay you $250 a whole day.

00:02:33.618 --> 00:02:35.132
That's not money.

00:02:35.132 --> 00:02:38.604
There's prestige in it,
but that's not money.

00:02:38.604 --> 00:02:42.602
Advertising, cosmetic contracts,
that's where the money is.

00:02:42.602 --> 00:02:44.353
That's where they may
pay you half a million,

00:02:44.353 --> 00:02:46.114
million dollars for jobs.

00:02:46.114 --> 00:02:47.020
That's what I wanted.

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:48.536
I wanted that "spoils of war".

00:02:48.536 --> 00:02:49.519
(laughs)
- [Interviewer] Yeah?

00:02:49.519 --> 00:02:51.557
- Yeah. And, that's what I fought for.

00:02:51.557 --> 00:02:53.506
- Was it out of, and I don't
mean this disrespectful,

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:54.633
but was it out of greed,

00:02:54.633 --> 00:02:56.447
or was it out of wanting to be valued?

00:02:56.447 --> 00:02:58.081
- As of our value system.

00:02:58.081 --> 00:03:00.290
If you are going to pay
that amount to another girl,

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:03.547
why couldn't you pay me for
the same service I provided?

00:03:03.547 --> 00:03:05.437
It's about that. It's about that.

00:03:05.437 --> 00:03:06.678
It's not about greed.

00:03:06.678 --> 00:03:10.866
Because usually people
who are about greed,

00:03:10.866 --> 00:03:12.110
they will prostitute themselves,

00:03:12.110 --> 00:03:14.695
they will do whatever
it takes to get there.

00:03:14.695 --> 00:03:17.804
And, my sense of value
was that I'll sit it out.

00:03:17.804 --> 00:03:19.588
Either they'll come my way or no way.

00:03:19.588 --> 00:03:21.895
Failure, to me, I'm not scared of it

00:03:21.895 --> 00:03:25.092
because it just gives me the
opportunity to for change.

00:03:25.092 --> 00:03:28.066
I think change is very good,

00:03:28.066 --> 00:03:30.548
regardless in what shape,
or form it comes into it.

00:03:30.548 --> 00:03:34.216
Because it makes you really observe

00:03:34.216 --> 00:03:37.374
and reorganize and rethink your life.

00:03:37.374 --> 00:03:40.071
- The Project Runway Canada
thing, what I wanted is,

00:03:40.071 --> 00:03:41.329
like, obviously very different scenario

00:03:41.329 --> 00:03:42.294
from where you started.

00:03:42.294 --> 00:03:44.315
But, when you see these people
who are trying to break in,

00:03:44.315 --> 00:03:45.564
you watch the whole experience.

00:03:45.564 --> 00:03:48.417
You see them from a perspective
that you understand,

00:03:48.417 --> 00:03:49.531
perhaps, all too well.

00:03:49.531 --> 00:03:50.541
- Absolutely.

00:03:50.541 --> 00:03:54.226
But, the funny part is that
it's a double-edged sword now.

00:03:54.226 --> 00:03:57.276
Because they become, like on this show,

00:03:57.276 --> 00:04:01.071
they could literally become
household names overnight.

00:04:01.071 --> 00:04:04.408
And, to forget that there is
hard work that comes with it,

00:04:04.408 --> 00:04:07.969
and just feel and believe
in the hype, so to speak,

00:04:07.969 --> 00:04:10.181
it will be their downfall.

00:04:10.181 --> 00:04:12.149
That would be their downfall.
- Did that ever happen to you?

00:04:12.149 --> 00:04:12.982
Or, you're walking around going,

00:04:12.982 --> 00:04:14.426
"I'm Iman."
- I believed-- oh yeah.

00:04:14.426 --> 00:04:16.280
Oh yeah. I'm the shit. (laughs)

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:17.313
(audience laughs)

00:04:17.313 --> 00:04:18.290
- [Interviewer] You can
say whatever you want.

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:20.840
- And then, and then, some
young girl comes in and

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:22.276
takes your place. (laughs)

00:04:22.276 --> 00:04:23.219
(audience laughs)

00:04:23.219 --> 00:04:24.796
There's always a young girl. (laughs)

00:04:24.796 --> 00:04:26.804
- I mean, it's such an
incredibly competitive industry

00:04:26.804 --> 00:04:28.393
on that level.
- It is. It is.

00:04:28.393 --> 00:04:32.386
But, what it makes, the
people who have, really,

00:04:32.386 --> 00:04:35.367
who have a sense of
like, this is a business,

00:04:35.367 --> 00:04:39.081
and how to learn very early
how you become the product.

00:04:39.081 --> 00:04:42.676
Don't wait for the job to come
to you, you create the job.

00:04:42.676 --> 00:04:46.039
Those are the only ones who
survive in the business.

00:04:46.039 --> 00:04:48.656
There's Cindy Crawford, Linda Evangelista,

00:04:48.656 --> 00:04:50.567
Tyra Banks, Heidi Klum.
- [Interviewer] Right.

00:04:50.567 --> 00:04:53.254
- Was it incredibly shell-shocking

00:04:53.254 --> 00:04:57.342
to go to Studio 54, to
New York, to sex, drugs,

00:04:57.342 --> 00:04:58.175
rock and roll, that world?
- Yeah.

00:04:58.175 --> 00:04:59.367
Yeah.
- What was it like?

00:04:59.367 --> 00:05:00.906
What kind of challenge was it,

00:05:00.906 --> 00:05:02.496
and how did you deal with that?

00:05:02.496 --> 00:05:04.651
- Oh, it wasn't a challenge.
I was 18. I was ready.

00:05:04.651 --> 00:05:06.297
(laughs)
- (laughs)

00:05:06.297 --> 00:05:07.934
- I was, "Bring more!"

00:05:07.934 --> 00:05:11.183
No, of course, I mean, you
know, I was 18 years old.

00:05:11.183 --> 00:05:13.279
And, one of the reasons I
came to the United States

00:05:13.279 --> 00:05:16.205
was actually to experience life.

00:05:16.205 --> 00:05:19.054
But, I had no idea what
I was getting into.

00:05:19.054 --> 00:05:21.730
But, what saved me, I always say,

00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:24.416
is that I've always known
when to leave the party.

00:05:24.416 --> 00:05:26.349
I never stayed the party
too long, you know?

00:05:26.349 --> 00:05:28.270
There's a time and a place for it.

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:31.182
And, in this industry,

00:05:31.182 --> 00:05:33.589
modeling, it is really, really critic

00:05:33.589 --> 00:05:37.029
that you are very professional,
to show up on time.

00:05:37.029 --> 00:05:38.145
And, everything you do,

00:05:38.145 --> 00:05:40.021
whether it's sex, drugs, or rock and roll,

00:05:40.021 --> 00:05:41.712
it will show on your face.

00:05:41.712 --> 00:05:43.830
So, it is moderation,

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:46.330
and when to know when it's enough

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:48.864
and when it's really to
be serious about business.

00:05:48.864 --> 00:05:50.875
It's been fun. (laughs)
- (laughs)

00:05:50.875 --> 00:05:52.311
- [Interviewer] Coming from modeling,

00:05:52.311 --> 00:05:54.335
where does the business
background come from?

00:05:54.335 --> 00:05:55.700
I mean, there are other models

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:58.219
who have tried to turn something else,

00:05:58.219 --> 00:06:00.033
but you've developed a full business.

00:06:00.033 --> 00:06:02.003
Did that just come along the way?

00:06:02.003 --> 00:06:05.763
- I think, most of it, it
was a natural progression.

00:06:05.763 --> 00:06:07.954
It wasn't something I
really thought about it

00:06:07.954 --> 00:06:09.897
and really thought it through,

00:06:09.897 --> 00:06:13.062
but everything of it has to be authentic.

00:06:13.062 --> 00:06:15.711
So, the cosmetics was a natural given

00:06:15.711 --> 00:06:19.340
because I could never
find cosmetics for myself

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:20.641
all the years I've modeled.

00:06:20.641 --> 00:06:22.596
So, that was a natural progression,

00:06:22.596 --> 00:06:25.474
because not only I was looking for one,

00:06:25.474 --> 00:06:27.338
but all women, women of skin of color,

00:06:27.338 --> 00:06:28.926
were asking me the same thing.

00:06:28.926 --> 00:06:33.173
So, IMAN Cosmetics, launching
it was really a natural.

00:06:33.173 --> 00:06:35.196
The other stuff was really passion.

00:06:35.196 --> 00:06:36.898
The IMAN Home is my passion.

00:06:36.898 --> 00:06:40.028
I love, I love interior decorating.

00:06:40.028 --> 00:06:42.734
So, that was really, truly just passion.

00:06:42.734 --> 00:06:45.040
And, the HSN Global Chic.

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:46.540
Because HSN came to me,

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:50.145
and I created a small
collection of accessories,

00:06:50.145 --> 00:06:52.714
and then it just became more and more,

00:06:52.714 --> 00:06:56.835
and now it's like the number
two fashion brand at HSN.

00:06:56.835 --> 00:07:01.002
- At this point in your career,
how do you judge success?

00:07:03.343 --> 00:07:07.060
- By what you inspire other people to do.

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:07.893
- Really?
- Yeah.

00:07:07.893 --> 00:07:09.863
I think that's what really success is.

00:07:09.863 --> 00:07:11.922
It's not what you
achieve or what you gain,

00:07:11.922 --> 00:07:15.626
it's what you really
inspire other peoples to do.

00:07:15.626 --> 00:07:17.066
- Did you always see it that way?

00:07:17.066 --> 00:07:17.940
In the beginning of your career,

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:19.568
would you have answered
that question the same way?

00:07:19.568 --> 00:07:22.486
- No. It would have all
been about me. (laughs)

00:07:22.486 --> 00:07:23.319
- (laughs)

00:07:23.319 --> 00:07:24.427
- What's in it for me?

00:07:24.427 --> 00:07:25.794
It would have been that, yeah.

00:07:25.794 --> 00:07:27.412
- What made that change then for you?

00:07:27.412 --> 00:07:29.120
- I think age.

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:32.952
You accumulate some kind of a wisdom.

00:07:32.952 --> 00:07:36.568
You see how you affect
other people's lives

00:07:36.568 --> 00:07:40.536
in small ways that become big ways.

00:07:40.536 --> 00:07:41.454
- Yeah.

00:07:41.454 --> 00:07:44.424
Self-esteem is a big issue.

00:07:44.424 --> 00:07:46.740
As little as it is.

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:48.730
And, as everybody thinks that,

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:52.704
especially pretty people,
or pretty girls, have it.

00:07:52.704 --> 00:07:56.151
And kids, you think, they are born with

00:07:56.151 --> 00:07:57.746
exuberance and innocence,

00:07:57.746 --> 00:08:00.884
but their self-esteem can
be taken away so easily.

00:08:00.884 --> 00:08:03.001
That simple thing that I do

00:08:03.001 --> 00:08:06.195
in my career as a model,

00:08:06.195 --> 00:08:10.502
and then especially as
CEO of IMAN Cosmetics,

00:08:10.502 --> 00:08:13.874
it's been really huge for me.

00:08:13.874 --> 00:08:16.507
It galvanized a whole
generation of young girls

00:08:16.507 --> 00:08:18.809
to think of themselves differently.

00:08:18.809 --> 00:08:21.428
So, to me, that is, you know,

00:08:21.428 --> 00:08:23.091
that is an inspiration to me

00:08:23.091 --> 00:08:26.140
to see people, young girls, changing

00:08:26.140 --> 00:08:28.324
right in front of my eyes as they grow up,

00:08:28.324 --> 00:08:31.600
and saying, "Yeah, yeah,
I am too beautiful. Yeah."

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:34.769
I started IMAN Cosmetics in 1994.

00:08:34.769 --> 00:08:37.646
So, I, when I was creating IMAN Cosmetics,

00:08:37.646 --> 00:08:40.757
to me, I wanted to have a new language.

00:08:40.757 --> 00:08:42.420
I didn't want the old mentality

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:44.378
that the whole world is black and white,

00:08:44.378 --> 00:08:46.368
because the world is not black and white.

00:08:46.368 --> 00:08:48.712
There's a lot of different
shades in between.

00:08:48.712 --> 00:08:50.899
And so, I wanted to create a new product,

00:08:50.899 --> 00:08:54.755
a new language, for people
to address what beauty is.

00:08:54.755 --> 00:08:57.943
And, in 1994, when I
created IMAN Cosmetics,

00:08:57.943 --> 00:08:59.737
it was the first company

00:08:59.737 --> 00:09:02.606
that was truly multicultural

00:09:02.606 --> 00:09:05.118
and, you know, truly global

00:09:05.118 --> 00:09:07.803
in terms of all the skin
tones that we were covering.

00:09:07.803 --> 00:09:10.331
We started first in America and Canada.

00:09:10.331 --> 00:09:13.438
Now, we're also in Europe,

00:09:13.438 --> 00:09:16.892
in London, I mean, in England, in France.

00:09:16.892 --> 00:09:20.851
I remember as young as seven, eight,

00:09:20.851 --> 00:09:23.273
my mom telling me,
"Always know your worth,

00:09:23.273 --> 00:09:25.305
"don't ever settle for less."

00:09:25.305 --> 00:09:29.152
So, that is what I came
to this country with.

00:09:29.152 --> 00:09:31.826
So, I was the first model who
said, "I'm not going to do

00:09:31.826 --> 00:09:34.006
any job unless I get
paid the same amount."

00:09:34.006 --> 00:09:36.710
Because to me, it was just,
I'm providing a service.

00:09:36.710 --> 00:09:39.102
So what has that got anything to do with?

00:09:39.102 --> 00:09:41.552
I wrote, "I am Iman",

00:09:41.552 --> 00:09:45.173
which was a book that really
addressed my working life

00:09:45.173 --> 00:09:47.772
as a model, in 2000.

00:09:47.772 --> 00:09:49.369
And, for years and years, of course,

00:09:49.369 --> 00:09:51.427
owning a cosmetic company,

00:09:51.427 --> 00:09:53.650
publishers have asked me
to write a beauty book.

00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:56.964
So, I thought, really, who I
want to write this book is for

00:09:56.964 --> 00:10:00.461
like, the generation of my
daughter who is nine years old,

00:10:00.461 --> 00:10:02.121
who is a multi-racial.

00:10:02.121 --> 00:10:04.716
So, the book is called,
"The Beauty of Color".

00:10:04.716 --> 00:10:05.874
When you look at the book,

00:10:05.874 --> 00:10:07.706
there is the pictures of
these beautiful girls,

00:10:07.706 --> 00:10:12.084
but on the side is their name
and their country of origin,

00:10:12.084 --> 00:10:14.047
and I wanted to celebrate that.

00:10:14.047 --> 00:10:16.791
So, I wanted, really, to
create a book that really

00:10:16.791 --> 00:10:19.304
celebrated, and a way to show it,

00:10:19.304 --> 00:10:22.056
that we are here, and
we are very beautiful.

00:10:22.056 --> 00:10:24.239
(upbeat music)

00:10:24.239 --> 00:10:25.586
- Thank you so much for watching.

00:10:25.586 --> 00:10:26.657
I made this video because

00:10:26.657 --> 00:10:29.280
Love, God &amp; Tattoos asked me to.

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:30.467
So, if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:10:30.467 --> 00:10:32.241
that you want me to profile next,

00:10:32.241 --> 00:10:34.665
leave it in the comments below,
and I'll see what I can do.

00:10:34.665 --> 00:10:37.074
I'd also love to know which
of Iman's top ten rules

00:10:37.074 --> 00:10:38.472
meant the most to you.

00:10:38.472 --> 00:10:41.237
You're going to now go out and
make a difference in your life.

00:10:41.237 --> 00:10:43.143
Leave in the comments, I'll
join in the discussion.

00:10:43.143 --> 00:10:44.643
Thank you so much for watching.

00:10:44.643 --> 00:10:47.197
Continue to believe,
and I'll see you soon.

00:10:47.197 --> 00:10:49.760
(rocket blasting)

